# loops: pseudo-instructions a target states as data, expanded into their
# steps after allocation, see doc/machine/loop.md
#
# an operation no instruction and no straight-line expansion does, as a
# read-modify-write through a load-reserved and store-conditional pair, is
# selected to a target's loop with its operands, scratch registers and
# parameters stated. once allocation and the frame have placed them, the expansion
# writes each loop's steps, its body a block of its own, reading nothing but
# the loop's row.

